=== REASONING ===
battery-cells.json:
  - fn_battery_cell_readings returned fake per-cell data derived from BrickVoltageMax/Min aggregates.
    Fleet Telemetry provides only pack-level aggregates (BrickVoltageMax, BrickVoltageMin, ModuleTempMax, ModuleTempMin).
    No way to reconstruct individual cell readings. Panels DISABLED with ADR-002 explanation.
  - fn_battery_cell_balance computed voltage_delta = max - min across cells.
    This IS available directly: BrickVoltageMax - BrickVoltageMin from signal_log.
    REWRITTEN with FILTER aggregate query on signal_log with time + signal filters.
  - fn_battery_cell_temp_heatmap returned per-cell temperature over time.
    Only ModuleTempMax/Min available — no per-cell breakdown. DISABLED.

battery-degradation.json:
  - fn_battery_soh_trend: SoH% over time. Estimated as (EnergyRemaining / BatteryLevel * 100)
    normalized to max observed capacity = 100%. Uses time_bucket('1 day') for daily aggregation.
    Window function MAX() OVER() for normalization baseline.
  - fn_battery_capacity_over_time: Returns estimated_capacity + original_capacity time series.
    estimated_capacity = EnergyRemaining / (BatteryLevel/100) daily.
    original_capacity = MAX(estimated_capacity) OVER() as reference line.
  - fn_battery_charge_cycles: Simple COUNT(*) from charging_sessions per vehicle.
    Original computed cumulative energy / nominal capacity, but without known nominal capacity,
    session count is the honest metric.
  - fn_battery_degradation_rate: Annual degradation % from linear regression (regr_slope)
    on estimated capacity over time. Slope converted from per-second to per-year and
    expressed as percentage of average capacity.
  - fn_battery_risk_factors: Required 4 composite risk scores (fast-charge ratio,
    high-SoC frequency, temperature exposure, deep discharge). Each needs complex
    cross-table business logic. Too complex for inline Grafana SQL → DISABLED.

All signal_log queries include: vehicle_id filter, signal IN filter, created_at time range.
No value_text (using value_num). No signal_name (using signal). No ts (using created_at).

